          essay: `The question of whether university canteens should be open to the public has sparked a heated debate. Personally, I believe that opening canteens to the public could lead to a series of issues. Firstly, it may compromise the dining experience for students. With an influx of outsiders, queues could become longer and seating more scarce, disrupting the tranquility that students need for a relaxed meal. Moreover, the primary purpose of university canteens is to cater to the dietary needs of students and staff, not to generate profit. Allowing the general public to dine in could divert resources from the campus community. In conclusion, while the idea of inclusivity is commendable, the practical implications of opening university canteens to the public outweigh the benefits. It is crucial to prioritize the well-being and convenience of the university community.`,
